# Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Project Auris in your research, teaching, or portfolio, please cite it as below."
title: "Project Auris: FPGA-Accelerated Assistive Audio Platform"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: <LAST_NAME>
    given-names: <FIRST_NAME>
    affiliation: "Project Auris"
    email: "<you>@example.com"
license: MIT
license-url: https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/<OWNER>/project-auris
url: https://github.com/<OWNER>/project-auris
abstract: |
  Project Auris is an open-source hearing-assistive platform built around a
  Xilinx Spartan-7 FPGA that performs real-time spectral audio processing.
  A 256-point FFT pipeline applies user-configurable per-bin gain profiles,
  noise gating, and dynamic range compression for hearing-loss compensation
  and speech enhancement. The repository includes the SystemVerilog RTL
  for the FPGA, Python code generators for window coefficients and
  audiogram-derived gain tables, schematics and a bill of materials for
  the reference hardware, and the full design documentation that
  accompanies the project from skeleton to minimum viable product.
keywords:
  - fpga
  - hearing-aid
  - dsp
  - fft
  - open-source-hardware
  - signal-processing
  - xilinx-spartan-7
